        {
          "path": "_m/9/w/s/b/rio-grande-del-norte-national-monument-wk/mypubliclandsroadtrip-2016-wil.jpg",
          "filename": "-mypubliclandsroadtrip 2016- Wildlife Watching, Rio Grande del Norte National Monument (28360608204).jpg",
          "caption": "The Río Grande del Norte National Monument in New Mexico is comprised of rugged, wide open plains at an average elevation of 7,000 feet, dotted by volcanic cones. The Río Grande carves an 800 foot deep gorge through layers of volcanic basalt flows and ash. The monument is an important area for wintering animals, and provides a corridor by which wildlife move between the mountain ranges.\nPhoto by Bob Wick, BLM",
